1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,892
Hand embroidery takes hours.

2
00:00:01,912 --> 00:00:03,757
One wrong wash can ruin it.

3
00:00:03,777 --> 00:00:05,470
Here’s how to wash it right.

4
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:07,062
First, test the colours.

5
00:00:07,082 --> 00:00:09,560
Dab a hidden stitch with a damp white cloth.

6
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,037
Turn it inside out.

7
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:12,277
Use cold water.

8
00:00:12,297 --> 00:00:14,557
Hot water makes threads bleed and shrink.

9
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:16,743
Add a few drops of mild detergent.

10
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:17,810
No bleach.

11
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:18,901
Swish gently.

12
00:00:18,921 --> 00:00:20,707
Never scrub. Never wring.

13
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:23,060
Rinse in cool water till it runs clear.

14
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:25,560
Roll it in a towel and press the water out.

15
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,049
Dry it flat, in the shade.

16
00:00:27,069 --> 00:00:28,560
Sunlight fades thread.

17
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:32,435
Iron on the reverse, over a towel, so the stitches stay raised.

18
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:33,678
Caps and bags?

19
00:00:33,698 --> 00:00:35,765
Just spot clean with a damp cloth.

20
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:38,239
Be gentle, and it will last for years.

21
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,915
Save this for wash day.

